## Oracle finding

Pinned Java `ProcessQueue.putMessage([message, null])` inserts the valid prefix
and increments `msgSize` before the null dereference. It throws before applying
the local valid count, setting dispatch state, or parsing the last message's
`MAX_OFFSET`. Rust's `put_message_items_nullable` preserves those partial
mutations and returns `ProcessQueueError::NullMessageElement`.

The invoked Java fixture and Rust facade test check the immediate count, size,
and tree, then verify the next valid insertion dispatches and counts normally.
Fixture SHA-256:
`01133da592b2f5c73b5fb379e14626651887cf8c0543875b928f266f02221aa1`.

